["11:06"]={"\00311:06\004 And … oh. The ironing. What am I going to do about that?","The Undomestic Goddess","Sophie Kinsella"},
["11:07"]={"“Yes.” Perena’s firm tone brooked no argument. “It exploded at \00311:07\004. You would have entered at 11:02, so that by then you would have been exactly midway between the Gates.”","The Shadow and Night","Chris Walley"},
["11:08"]={"He glanced up so that he could see the time on the datastrip along the upper edge of his helmet: \00311:08\004:23. Ten minutes. They walked unsteadily on.","The Infinite Day","Chris Walley"},
["11:09"]={"The last was October 12 at \00311:09 a.m.\004\n“It took him all of five weeks,” I said. “Except…” The words wouldn’t come out. In fact, I was afraid if I opened my mouth I would throw up.","NYPD Red 3","James Patterson"},
["11:10"]={"She backed down the driveway, checked for traffic, and turned toward the turnpike. \003Ten past eleven\004. Plenty of time.\nThat’s what she thought then.","If It Bleeds","Stephen King"},
["11:11"]={"The LCD face on his Super G Digital Athletic Chronometer blinks, \00311:11\004, on and off and on and off. Eleven eleven. Eleven eleven. Eleven eleven.","The Indifference League","Richard Scarsbrook"},
["11:12"]={"\00311:12\004 I have a solution, via the local paper. A girl from the village will collect it, iron it all overnight at £3 a shirt, and sew on Eddie’s button.","The Undomestic Goddess","Sophie Kinsella"},
["11:13"]={"The first time I saw them it was \003around eleven, eleven-fifteen\004, a Saturday morning, I was about two thirds through my route when I turned onto their block and noticed a ’56 Ford sedan pulled up in the yard with a big open U-Haul behind.","Where I’m Calling From","Raymond Carver"},
["11:14"]={"When they’d finished their burgers, Melissa glanced at her watch, a big plastic digital thing that looked like it should belong to a child.\n“\003Eleven fourteen\004,” Melissa said. “We’ve still got forty-four minutes to kill before the end of the world.”","The Glass Hotel","Emily St. John Mandel"},
["11:15"]={"Have you a couple of days to spare? Have just been wired for from the west of England in connection with Boscombe Valley tragedy. Shall be glad if you will come with me. Air and scenery perfect. Leave Paddington by the \00311:15\004.","The Adventures of Sherlock Holmes","Sir Arthur Conan Doyle"},
["11:16"]={"Eventually, at \00311:16\004, he did show up, and took his reserved place at the baccarat table. Stephen stopped sipping his tomato juice and Jean-Pierre moved over and waited patiently by the table for one of the men seated on the left or right of Harvey to leave.","Not a Penny More, Not a Penny Less","Jeffrey Archer"},
["11:17"]={"Ted presented himself at the front door of Number 10 at \00311:17\004 the next day. The deputy clerk accompanied him down the long corridor to the ground floor and asked him to take a seat in the small waiting area that adjoins the Cabinet Room.","Shoeshine Boy","Jeffrey Archer"},
["11:18"]={"It is \00311:18\004. A row of bungalows in a round with a clump of larch tree in the middle.","Trumpet","Jackie Kay"},
["11:19"]={"A whistle cut sharply across his words. Peter got onto his knees to look out the window, and Miss Fuller glared at him. Polly looked down at her watch: \00311:19\004. The train. But the stationmaster had said it was always late.","Blackout","Connie Willis"},
["11:20"]={"Sweeney pointed to the clock above the bar, held in the massive and indifferent jaws of a stuffed alligator head. The time was \00311:20\004.","American Gods","Neil Gaiman"},
["11:21"]={"It was \003twenty-one minutes past eleven\004 by the clock over the elevator doors when Joel Cairo came in from the street. His forehead was bandaged. His clothes had the limp unfreshness of too many hours’ consecutive wear.","The Maltese Falcon","Dashiell Hammett"},
["11:23"]={"The music was almost raucous. She turned it off. She lay in silence, waiting for sleep. It was \00311:23 a.m.\004","The Black Corridor","Michael Moorcock"},
["11:24"]={"At \00311:24\004 we thanked Helen Gillard and asked her to thank the doctor for us, left the house, walked sixty yards to Wolfe’s, found the door was bolted, pushed the button and were admitted by Fritz.","The Final Deduction","Rex Stout"},
["11:25"]={"When, at about \00311:25 am\004, Katharina Blum was finally taken from her apartment for questioning, it was decided not to handcuff her at all.","The Lost Honour of Katharina Blum","Heinrich Böll"},
["11:26"]={"A pair of brown shoes appeared beneath his urine bag. “I counted eleven bells.”\n“The current time is \00311:26 AM\004.”\n“What day?”\n“Your injury occurred yesterday.”","The Wind Knot","John Galligan"},
["11:27"]={"Tom turned into Savoy Place at \003twenty-seven minutes past eleven\004, to face a fleet of stationary limousines disgorging their passengers outside the hotel.","Be Careful What You Wish For","Jeffrey Archer"},
["11:29"]={"You are four minutes too slow. No matter; it’s enough to mention the error. Now from this moment, \003twenty-nine minutes after eleven, a.m.\004, this Wednesday, 2nd October, you are in my service.","Around the World in Eighty Days","Jules Verne"},
["11:30"]={"“The extraordinary thing is,” he told Livia at \003eleven-thirty\004, “you seem to be the only applicant. Or at least, the only one who’s showed up.”","The Wedding Officer","Anthony Capella"},
["11:31"]={"Albatross 8 passed over Pamlico Sound at \0031131\004 local time. Its on-board programming was designed to trace thermal receptors over the entire visible horizon, interrogating everything in sight and locking on any signature that fit its acquisition parameters.","The Hunt for Red October","Tom Clancy"},
["11:32"]={"And after that, not forgetting, there was the Flemish armada, all scattered, and all officially drowned, there and then, on a lovely morning, after the universal flood, at about \003eleven thirty two\004 was it? Off the coast of Cominghome.","Finnegans Wake","James Joyce"},
["11:33"]={"At \00311:33\004 the sleek cream nose of an Aston Martin slid to a stop at the gate and Maurice Kemp-Lore stepped out. He stretched himself, stiff from driving, and glanced over the front of the cottage.","Nerve","Dick Francis"},
["11:34"]={"Christmas Eve 1995. \00311:34 am\004. The first time, Almasa says it slowly and softly, as if she is really looking for an answer, “Are you talking to me?” She peers into the small, grimy mirror in a train toilet.","How to Fare Well and Stay Fair","Adnan Mahmutovic"},
["11:35"]={"At \00311:35\004 the Colonel came out; he looked hot and angry as he strode towards the lift. There goes a hanging judge, thought Wormold.","Our Man in Havana","Graham Greene"},
["11:36"]={"I ran up the stairs, away from the heat and the noise, the mess and the confusion. I saw the clock radio by my bed. \003Eleven thirty-six\004.","Losing You","Nicci French"},
["11:37"]={"At \003eleven thirty-seven\004 I handed over the full and final settlement to Mr. Fothergill in exchange for the freehold of Number 1 Chelsea Terrace.","As the Crow Flies","Jeffrey Archer"},
["11:38"]={"At \00311:38\004, she left her desk and walked to the side door of the auditorium, arriving ten minutes before noon.","The Circle","Dave Eggers"},
["11:39"]={"After painstaking ticket-office conversations and timetable consultations, I established with as much certainty as any tourist can hope for that the \00311:39\004 to Paris Est was a service on which accompanied bicycles could be carried free of charge.","French Revolutions","Tim Moore"},
["11:40"]={"There was a group of about twenty people waiting for the \00311:40\004 train, and the murderess and her daughter walked some fifty yards farther down the platform and stood alone, not speaking.","Innocent Blood","P.D. James"},
["11:41"]={"Giles turned to see the dean standing by his side. He bowed. It must be \00311:41\004.","This Was a Man","Jeffrey Archer"},
["11:42"]={"The front door opens. Her heart pounds. She looks at the time on the bottom right of her screen. \00311:42\004.","The Woman Downstairs","Elisabeth Carpenter"},
["11:43"]={"\003Eleven-forty-three\004. In four minutes, give or take, Emma would die.","Blood Rites","Jim Butcher"},
["11:44"]={"Weiss’s watch said \003sixteen minutes to twelve\004, and the detonation was set for noon, as set by a bank of electric clocks and three seperate control cables. But when the dragon embraced the bomb and tightened his grip, it was enough.","To Hold the Bridge","Garth Nix"},
["11:45"]={"I waited till a \003quarter to twelve\004, and found then that I was in All Souls’. But I wasn’t much frightened, for I thought it could be tomorrow as well.","Far From the Maddening Crowd","Thomas Hardy"},
["11:48"]={"Well, you better go back with me. They’ll be mighty glad to see you.\n“We can make that \003eleven-forty-eight\004 if we hurry,” he said. “I’ll have to change a few things.”","The Wrong Twin","Harry Leon Wilson"},
["11:49"]={"Richie hadn’t made any outgoing calls after \00311:49 A.M.\004 However, there was a long list of incoming calls that afternoon, calls he would never return.","After All These Years","Susan Isaacs"},
["11:50"]={"The man who gave them to him handed him a ten-shilling note and promised him another if it were delivered at exactly \003ten minutes to twelve\004.","The Adventure of Johnnie Waverley: A Hercule Poirot Story","Agatha Christie"},
["11:51"]={"The next day, at \003nine minutes to twelve\004 o’clock noon, the last clock ran down and stopped. It was then placed in the town museum, as a collector’s item, or museum piece, with proper ceremonies, addresses, and the like.","Lanterns & Lances","James Thurber"},
["11:52"]={"At any rate, we whirled into the station with many more, just as the great clock pointed to \003eight minutes to twelve\004 o’clock. “Thank God! We are in time,” said the young man, “and thank you, too, my friend, and your good horse.”","Black Beauty","Anna Sewell"},
["11:53"]={"Afterward it was recalled by observing citizens that just before noon — \003seven minutes to twelve\004, in fact — a small cloud no bigger than the proverbial hand crossed the sun hurriedly as if afraid to tarry.","The Daughter of Anderson Crow","George Barr McCutcheon"},
["11:54"]={"He swilled off the remains of [his beer] and looked at the clock. It was \003six minutes to twelve\004.","Hangover Square","Patrick Hamilton"},
["11:55"]={"He was tearing off on his bicycle to one of the jobs about \003five minutes to twelve\004 to see if he could catch anyone leaving off for dinner before the proper time.","The Ragged Trousered Philanthropists","Robert Tressell"},
["11:56"]={"Aaron checked his watch on the run: \003four minutes to twelve\004. He prayed that Harry would be late. Harry was never late.","Cometh the Hour","Jeffrey Archer"},
["11:57"]={"I wondered what the time is? said the latter after a pause.\n“I don’t know exactly”, replied Easton, “but it \003can’t be far-off twelve\004.”","The Ragged Trousered Philanthropists","Robert Tressell"},
